                                 returns EC_GENERATION_DESCRIPTOR unsupported.
generation_descriptor.rs:592-604 V3 branch decodes the cover, then requires
                                 `descriptor.digest()? == expected_digest`, i.e.
                                 the embedded digest is verified, not trusted.
generation_descriptor.rs:512-515 validate() runs `payload_cover.validate()` AND
                                 `validate_row_schema(&self.row_schema)`, and
                                 decode() calls validate() at :622 before return.

RESULT: with payload_cover = None the emitted byte string is field-for-field
identical to base (the diff leaves every put_* call as context and only replaces
the version literal with `self.version()`). A covered descriptor is a strict
suffix append under a distinct leading version. Decode of either version
re-encodes canonically because every added field is fixed-width or
length-prefixed.


